depend. Browning writes about that somewhere; but our own senses will imagine them for

205
00:17:50,599 --> 00:17:56,200
us. There are moments when the odor of Leela blanc passes suddenly across me,

206
00:17:56,200 --> 00:17:59,957
and I have to live the strangest month of my life over

207
00:17:59,957 --> 00:18:04,957
again. I wish I could change places with you, Dorian. The world has cried out

208
00:18:04,957 --> 00:18:11,317
against us both, but it has always worshiped you. It always will worship you.

209
00:18:11,317 --> 00:18:16,398
You are the type of what the age is searching for, and what it is afraid it has

210
00:18:16,398 --> 00:18:21,759
found I'm so glad that you have never done anything, never carved a statue, or

211
00:18:21,759 --> 00:18:26,957
painted a picture, or produced anything outside of yourself! Life has been your

212
00:18:26,957 --> 00:18:34,240
art. You have set yourself to music. Your days are your sonnets.” Dorian rose up from the piano

213
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:39,398
and passed his hand through his hair. “Yes, life has been exquisite,” he

214
00:18:39,398 --> 00:18:44,439
murmured, “but I'm not going to have the same life, Harry. And you must not say

215
00:18:44,439 --> 00:18:49,599
these extravagant things to me. You don’t know everything about me. I think that if

216
00:18:49,599 --> 00:18:57,599
you did, even you would turn from me. You laugh. Don’t laugh.” “Why have you stopped playing,

217
00:18:57,599 --> 00:18:59,080
Dorian?

218
00:18:59,080 --> 00:19:03,637
Go back and give me the nocturn over again. Look at that great honey colored

219
00:19:03,637 --> 00:19:08,360
moon that hangs in the dusky air she's waiting for you to charm her, and if you

220
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:10,878
play she will come closer to the earth.

221
00:19:10,878 --> 00:19:14,878
You won’t? Let us go to the club, then. It has

222
00:19:14,878 --> 00:19:20,080
been a charming evening, and we must end it charmingly. There is someone at Whit's

223
00:19:20,080 --> 00:19:26,240
who wants immensely to know you— —young Lord P Bournemouth’s eldest son he's

224
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:31,317
already copied your neck ties and has begged me to introduce him to you. He is

225
00:19:31,317 --> 00:19:37,119
quite delightful and rather reminds me of you.” “I hope not,” said Dorian with a sad

226
00:19:37,119 --> 00:19:39,759
look in his eyes. “But I am tired tonight

227
00:19:39,759 --> 00:19:42,599
Harry. I sh go to the club. It is nearly

228
00:19:42,599 --> 00:19:48,159
11: and I want to go to bed early.” “Do stay. You have never played so well as

229
00:19:48,159 --> 00:19:52,279
tonight There was something in your touch that was wonderful. It had more

230
00:19:52,279 --> 00:19:57,398
expression than I had ever heard from it before.” “It is because I am going to be

231
00:19:57,398 --> 00:20:02,797
good,” he answered, smiling. “I am a little changed already.”

232
00:20:02,797 --> 00:20:09,279
“You cannot change to me, Dorian,” said Lord Henry. “You and I will always be friends.”

233
00:20:09,279 --> 00:20:15,159
“Yet you poisoned me with a book once. I should not forgive that. Harry, promise me

234
00:20:15,159 --> 00:20:22,119
that you will never lend that book to anyone It does harm.” “My dear boy, you are really

235
00:20:22,119 --> 00:20:27,080
beginning to moralize. You will soon be going about like the converted, and the

236
00:20:27,080 --> 00:20:32,477
revivalist, warning people against all the sins of which you have grown tired.

237
00:20:32,477 --> 00:20:35,680
You are much too delightful to do that.

238
00:20:35,680 --> 00:20:42,919
Besides, it is no use. You and I are what we are, and will be what we will

239
00:20:42,919 --> 00:20:48,680
be. As for being poisoned by a book, there is no such thing as that. Art has no

240
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:54,759
influence upon action. It annihilates the desire to act. It is superbly sterile. The

241
00:20:54,759 --> 00:20:59,360
books that the world calls immoral are books that show the world its own shame.

242
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:06,398
That is all. But we won’t discuss literature. Come around tomorrow I'm going to ride at

243
00:21:06,398 --> 00:21:12,200
11: We might go together, and I will take you to lunch afterwards with Lady branom

244
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:15,957
She is a charming woman, and wants to consult you about some tapestries she's

245
00:21:15,957 --> 00:21:21,718
thinking of buying. Mind you come. Or shall we lunch with our little duchess?

246
00:21:21,718 --> 00:21:28,840
She says she never sees you now. Perhaps you are tired of Gladis I thought you would be.

247
00:21:28,840 --> 00:21:31,558
Her clever tongue gets on one’s nerves.

248
00:21:31,558 --> 00:21:37,477
Well, in any case, be here at 11: Must I really come,

249
00:21:37,477 --> 00:21:42,957
Harry?” “Certainly. The park is quite lovely now. I don’t think there have been such

250
00:21:42,957 --> 00:21:49,080
lilacs since the year I met you.” “Very well. I shall be here at 11: said Dorian.

251
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:54,797
“Good night, Harry.” As he reached the door, he hesitated for a moment, as if he had

252
00:21:54,797 --> 00:22:01,000
something more to say. Then he sighed and went out out dsh chapter
